      "side": 1,
      "message": "Computing `isControl8` (normalizing the text range and querying `codeUnitHasProperty` for each code unit) runs unconditionally for every glyph in the run. On normal text where almost all glyphs are resolved (`glyph !\u003d 0`), this adds unnecessary work on the hot shaping path.\n\nCould we short-circuit this to check `isControl8` only when `glyph \u003d\u003d 0`?\n```cpp\nbool glyphResolved \u003d glyph !\u003d 0;\nif (!glyphResolved) {\n    TextRange textRange \u003d normalizeTextRange(GlyphRange(i, i + 1));\n    bool isControl8 \u003d true;\n    for (TextIndex ch \u003d textRange.start; ch \u003c textRange.end; ++ch) {\n        if (!fParagraph-\u003ecodeUnitHasProperty(ch, SkUnicode::CodeUnitFlags::kControl)) {\n            isControl8 \u003d false;\n            break;\n        }\n    }\n    glyphResolved \u003d isControl8;\n}\n```",
      "revId": "db91c9a98c42b313133a8f00454dce010a2f74d8",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    }
